Install and update (macOS)
--------------------------
Open the .dmg and drag BLiNX1.app to Applications, replacing the
old one for an update. The game files are inside the app. To uninstall,
drag the app to the Trash; your saves stay in Application Support.

The app is signed ad hoc on the Mac that built it, not notarized. On
another Mac, Gatekeeper may refuse it: right-click > Open once, or run
  xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/BLiNX1.app

To keep saves and settings somewhere else, set BLINX1_DATA_DIR
to that folder before starting the game.

Options
-------
Your options live in config/config.toml in
~/Library/Application Support/BLiNX1. The app's
Contents/Resources/config.default.toml lists every option at its default.
Copy a line from it into your config.toml and change it there, for
example "scale = 2" under "[render]" to draw at twice the resolution. An
update replaces config.default.toml but never touches your file.

F10 (or Guide+A, an Elite controller's P1, or Back+L3 held for a moment)
opens the in-game menu to change these options while you play; F3 shows
the frame-rate strip. "enabled = false" under "[menu]" turns the menu
off.

